= Max Seydewitz

Max Seydewitz is a former leader of the youth wing, current supporter of the left wing of the <span style="color: #30B24A;">**egk**</span>, and advocates for class struggle.

- @class_struggle
- @socialist_youth
- @against_toleration
- @root: Return to main

@class_struggle
title: Rally for class struggle
subtitle: The core of <span style="color: #30B24A;">socialism</span> should be the struggle of the proletariat against the bourgeoisie.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; workers_egk += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_egk += 3*(1-dissent); workers_egk += 4*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress > 0; unemployed_egk += 3*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress > 0; left_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 5; old_middle_egk -= 3; new_middle_egk -= 2; dvp_relation -= 3; dvp_right += 1; lvp_relation -= 3; lvp_right += 1

Our message of class struggle appeals to the left wing of the working class, while potentially alienating the middle class. [? if nationalization_progress > 0 : Our achievements in nationalization have assisted our messaging. ?]


@socialist_youth
title: Support the <span style="color: #30B24A;">Socialist</span> Youth
subtitle: We must end our reputation as a party for old men by increasing funding to the youth organizations. -1 resources
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?] [? if resources <= 0 : Not enough resources. ?]
